From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:53:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the ordinality column index as an optional_idx while the binder builds it

Binder::BindTableFunctionInternal() declares ordinality_column_id as
an idx_t, assigns it only on the WITH ORDINALITY path, and hands it to
the scan's ordinality_idx, an optional_idx, afterwards. The compiler
cannot see that the read is reached only when the assignment was, and
-Wmaybe-uninitialized reports the index as possibly uninitialized
inside optional_idx's constructor. It is an optional_idx from the
start, as upstream makes it a few commits later: unset until the
ORDINALITY path sets it, and copied as it is.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp
index 528478c58b..4d2a476299 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp
@@ -193,7 +193,7 @@ BoundStatement Binder::BindTableFunctionInternal(TableFunction &table_function,
 	vector<string> return_names;
 	auto constexpr ordinality_name = "ordinality";
 	string ordinality_column_name = ordinality_name;
-	idx_t ordinality_column_id;
+	optional_idx ordinality_column_id;
 	if (table_function.bind || table_function.bind_replace || table_function.bind_operator) {
 		TableFunctionBindInput bind_input(parameters, named_parameters, input_table_types, input_table_names,
 		                                  table_function.function_info.get(), this, table_function, ref);
